<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 16 May, from 946 to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/japan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/japan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/946">946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,080 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Suzaku abdicates in favour of his brother Murakami</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor Suzaku, the 61st emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the traditional order of succession, abdicated in the 16th year of his reign. His younger brother Nariakira received the succession as Emperor Murakami, the 62nd emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/999">999 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,027 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mahmud of Ghazni defeats the Samanid army near Merv</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ghaznavid forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a> and his brother Abu'l Muzaffar Nasr, with cavalry and elephants, defeated the Samanid army of Abd al-Malik II near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merv">Merv</a>. The Samanid dynasty collapsed soon after, with the Kara-Khanid invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahmud-of-ghazni">Mahmud of Ghazni</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanid Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1204">1204 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">822 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Baldwin I is crowned first emperor of the Latin Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Baldwin, Count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, was crowned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a> as the first emperor of the Latin Empire. In 1205 the Bulgarian tsar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaloyan-of-bulgaria">Kaloyan</a> defeated and captured him at Adrianople.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baldwin-i-latin-emperor">Baldwin I, Latin Emperor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1364">1364 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">662 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bertrand du Guesclin defeats the Navarrese at Cocherel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>, a French army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin">Bertrand du Guesclin</a> defeated the Anglo-Navarrese army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-navarre">Charles II of Navarre</a>, called the Bad, at Cocherel. The battle was fought over the succession to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin">Bertrand du Guesclin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-navarre">Charles II of Navarre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1532">1532 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas More resigns as Lord Chancellor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after the clergy submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s authority, Sir Thomas More gave up the Great Seal. His refusal to accept the king's supremacy over the Church led to his execution in 1535.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1770">1770 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">256 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Antoinette marries the future Louis XVI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fourteen-year-old Austrian archduchess married the French dauphin at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, sealing an alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>. Both were guillotined during the Revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1868">1868 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Johnson escapes conviction by one vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate voted 35 to 19 to convict President Johnson on the first article tried, one vote short of the two-thirds needed. Johnson was the first US president to be impeached.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Academy Awards are presented in Hollywood</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 270 guests attended a dinner at the Hollywood Roosevelt Hotel where the first Oscars were handed out in around fifteen minutes. Wings won the top prize.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodore Maiman operates the first laser</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hughes Research Laboratories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, Maiman produced a pulse of red laser light from a ruby crystal. Lasers went on to transform medicine, communications and industry.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 May <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juan-rulfo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juan-rulfo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juan Rulfo</span><span class="tp">1917–1986</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/dawda-jawara"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/dawda-jawara.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Dawda Jawara</span><span class="tp">1924–2019</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 May <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-jin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-wu-of-jin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Wu of Jin</span><span class="tp">236–290</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-gibbon-wakefield"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-gibbon-wakefield.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Gibbon Wakefield</span><span class="tp">1796–1862</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/modibo-keita"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/modibo-keita.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Modibo Keïta</span><span class="tp">1915–1977</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bob-hawke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bob-hawke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bob Hawke</span><span class="tp">1929–2019</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
